WEBVTT

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:02.580
What do we do?

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:03.790
What do we do?

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.790
To be able to protect everyone?

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.830
Wait a minute! We're gonna talk it over

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.200
Grownups are so busy

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.330
So busy

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.330
We can't count on them

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.200
That's right

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.080
This town

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.160
We'll help it with Colors Power!

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.660
Pin-pin-pinches come suddenly

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:35.290
And so!

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:35.910
And so?

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:36.500
You know!

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.250
Gear up?

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:39.700
We have to stay on guard every day

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.120
It looks like our chance

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.250
Which is it?

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:44.750
I'm not sure!

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:45.370
Go on, think

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:45.950
But you know!

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:46.790
Basically

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:49.290
You don't know until you try

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.830
Peace of mind is far away

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.830
Is what I hear my heart say

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.330
Now be sneaky and bold

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.330
And do your best!

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:03.450
What times, what times, are the most fun?

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.620
We'll have to investigate more and more

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.950
Do grownups have the energy? They don't have energy

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.080
Kids have energy!

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.700
So leave it all to us!

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.830
We'll do our part with Colors Power!

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.450
Three-Stars Jump!

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:35.160
Colors

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.200
One-Coin Sat-chan, activate!

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.200
Hello, One-Coin Sat-chan!

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.500
Hewwo. I ahn Wa-Hoy Ha-han.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.040
That's right! You're One-Coin Sat-chan!

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.250
Hah hoo hree-ha-hed ee.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.540
That's right.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:56.000
We pooled all our New Year's money,

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:56.000
so we could buy a weapon for Colors.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.330
And we made the Colors Robot, One-Coin Sat-chan.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:02.700
But the memory transfer failed.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:06.660
Ohh. Hwa wa hwa hwa hwa hwa hwa hwa?

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.160
Huh? What?

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.500
Ghif hee eh ho-ho.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.410
I don't understand.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.040
Kotoha, did you get it?

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.200
No.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.620
At least let me talk like a normal person!

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.410
I can't see, but I can tell.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.750
We should never have done this.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.620
I'm sorry for dodging. I don't think it's gross.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.330
Then pick up the 500-yen coin.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.700
Anyway, let's go buy a good weapon, Sat-chan!

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.450
Pick it up.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:46.120
Pick up the coin.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.580
Uncle

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:54.200
Wow, this is awesome!

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.250
Look, look! They have knives! And pistols!

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.200
And shotguns! And bazookas!

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.700
It's a weapon store if I ever saw one!

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.290
You know about the most amazing places, Kotoha.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.080
I like it here.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.750
Where are the bazookas?

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.700
Oh! You're back, little girl!

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.160
You're working here again, Afro?

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.040
Uh, yeah, well...

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.370
What happened to your hair?

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.200
Did you get hit with a bazooka?

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:31.500
Yeah! I got shot with a bazooka! Pow!

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.950
Huh?

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:41.160
I do not like you.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.540
Huh? What'd I do?

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.330
We're here today to buy a weapon.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.000
A weapon, huh?

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.160
Unfortunately, I can't sell any to children. Sorry.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.450
This isn't a child! This is One-Coin Sat-chan!

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:55.290
Oh! Wait a second!

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:00.290
Hewwo. I ahn Wa-Hoy Ha-han.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.080
Uh, what's going on?

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.040
This is the Colors Robot! One-Coin Sat-chan!

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:10.370
Shouldn't it be "Three-Coin"?

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.450
I can't see, but I can tell.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:22.120
Oh, sorry. Reflex.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.910
I don't think it's gross.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.410
Then pick it up.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.500
Money is dirty, so you shouldn't put it in your mouth.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.950
Pick it up.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.410
Pick it up.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.700
Ueno Okachimachi Chudo-dori

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:42.910
Well, it's not exactly a weapon, but how about this?

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.080
Walkie-talkie.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.330
Walkie-talkie?

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.830
You mean like all the spies use?

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.910
Detectives use them a lot, too!

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.540
And champions of justice!

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.790
Yup, those are the ones.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.080
And hold on to your hats.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.370
This walkie-talkie...

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:05.000
comes in a set of red, blue, and yellow!

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.330
They do!

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.000
They were made for us!

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.290
I want them!

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:10.540
Me, too!

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:12.330
Then that's what we'll get!

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.250
You got it!

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.370
How much are they?

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.080
What?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.910
We have 1,500 yen!

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.250
You're going to pay? With money?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.790
Of course we are!

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.910
One-Coin Sat-chan will pay.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.040
One-Coin Sat-chan?

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:25.950
Huh?

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:28.120
Wait a minute.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.750
Why are we still doing this?

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.120
I ahn Wa-Hoy Ha-han.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.410
Wow.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.620
I haf fif-hee hun-huh hen.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.500
Perfect, these cost just 1,500 yen.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.200
Thanks for doing business!

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.500
I can't see, but I can tell!

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:47.790
Pops, that's gross!

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:48.790
Here you go!

00:05:50.750 --> 00:06:01.250
Yoruwara

00:05:50.750 --> 00:06:01.250
Ameyoko

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:53.500
Good luck with business this year, Pops!

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:56.250
Thanks! Good luck to you, too, Colors!

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.870
We don't need your luck!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.160
East Japan

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.370
This is Red. Over.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.750
This is Yellow!

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.370
I can hear you, Yui!

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.750
But Sat-chan, what about Kotoha?

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:22.080
Koto-chan, can't you hear her?

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:22.080
I can hear her! Koto-chan!

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:27.080
Aww. I can't hear her. Maybe she's too far away.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:30.040
Koto-chan, Yui says she can't hear you!

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:32.830
I'll try calling her.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.370
Koto-chan's saying the same thing!

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.290
Oh, hello, Kotoha?

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:44.040
I think you're out of range. Come back a little closer.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.080
...this?

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.750
Yeah! Oh, hey, I kind of heard you!

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.750
Koto-chan, I can see you now!

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:55.040
...ow's this?

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.790
A little more.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:01.040
Whoever came up with walkie-talkies is a genius!

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.250
Colors

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.540
Hegh ho hoo ha hrine.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.370
One-Coin Sat-chan has revived!

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:32.790
She's gotten a lot cheaper.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:34.290
Must be a production model.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.660
I think I like these 5-yen coins. I can see now!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:47.660
Is this why you told us each to bring five yen?

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.330
No, no!

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.950
I thought we could all make

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.950
our first shrine visit of the new year!

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.910
First shrine visit?

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:23.040
Do you think it's okay

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:23.040
to make a first shrine visit more than once?

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.450
I already went on New Year's Day.

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:29.700
Wait, is that bad? I already went with Mom.

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:33.950
There's no law saying you can't

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:33.950
make a first visit more than once.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:35.410
I think.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:39.200
Hanazono

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:39.200
Shrine

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.790
Okay. But it's not good to be greedy.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:43.290
So I'm gonna make the same wish

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:43.290
I made on New Year's Day.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.290
Good idea!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.250
Let's do it!

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.370
Offering

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:10.540
Hanazono

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:10.540
Inari

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:10.540
Shrine

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:14.040
May our town have peace for another year.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.750
Evil Overlord, come down to Earth...

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:19.330
...and please run amok in our town.

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.040
Huh? What are you wishing for?

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.040
That's a bad wish!

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.410
You're the one with a bad wish, Leader.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.370
Champions of Justice only exist

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.370
because there are bad guys.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:29.330
Indeed.

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:33.830
If bad guys ceased to exist,

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:33.830
that would mean the end of Colors.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:37.290
What? I-I don't want that!

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:43.830
Hanazono

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:43.830
Inari

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:43.830
Shrine

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:43.410
Evil Overlord, please run amok in our town!

00:09:49.330 --> 00:09:51.870
Now our town will be at peace.

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:54.000
What in the world?

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:58.410
Is that...?

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.330
It is! It's Colonel Monochrome!

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.040
I wonder what he's doing.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:04.410
Going on a walk?

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.620
Let's follow him!

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.160
Wait, Sat-chan!

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.000
If we're going to tail him,

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.000
we should be sneaky about it.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.620
Good point! Let's be sneaky!

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.120
Shh!

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:22.250
Now that I think of it, I don't know

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:22.250
what the Colonel does with all his time.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.250
Cats have many secrets.

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.750
We're gonna learn all your secrets today!

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:33.700
Shhhh!

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.080
Time for the

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.080
step-out-of-the-shadows-and-you're-dead game!

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.750
What? Really?

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.370
Ah! Koto-chan's dead!

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:46.160
I am un-killable.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:13.660
How far do you think the Colonel will go?

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:16.200
He might be contacting an evil organization.

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.750
He is a cat burglar.

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.790
Oh, that's possible!

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:21.950
Huh? New look, Yui?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.950
Huh? What do you mean?

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:30.910
Huh?

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:33.450
My tail's gone!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:35.950
That was a tail?

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.790
Did my hair tie fall out?

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:42.290
Uh-oh! We're losing the Colonel!

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:46.790
Ugh, wait for me!

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:01.120
Shimizu-zaka

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.040
Yui's back!

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.450
Oh, but you're not in the shadows. You're dead.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:20.000
I died forever ago! So what?!

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.870
Huh? Are you mad?

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:24.750
Where's the Colonel?

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:26.790
He went in there!

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.580
Back up! Back up!

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:46.950
He's going back.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.700
Did he take a wrong turn?

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:52.250
Why did I have to fall over, then?

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.910
If he keeps going this way...

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:59.500
What? We have to go up here?

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:01.200
Seventy-five steps.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.200
I thought it was seventy-six.

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.830
Which is it, Kotoha?

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:05.950
I don't know.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.160
There's actually something you don't know?

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.290
I avoid stairs in my life.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.790
Oh well! Guess we're climbing!

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:14.910
One.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:15.910
Two.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:17.080
Three.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.120
Four.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:19.000
Five.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:25.200
But wait.

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.540
I think this is the way to...

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.870
Yes, I'm sure of it now.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:39.330
The Colonel is heading for...

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:50.830
It's our hideout!

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:53.200
What was that all about, Colonel?

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:02.040
My hair tie!

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:03.790
Why?

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:05.870
Did you steal it?

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:09.250
When did you do that? You are a mystery, Colonel!

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.250
Oh! He's leaving again.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:14.790
I guess his private life is a secret.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.370
Next time, we will expose him!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.250
But not today. Too tired!

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.870
Colors

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.950
Those were yummy!

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.790
Cookies from a tin are a little stronger

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:05.790
than other cookies.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:08.500
But sometimes you do get some duds.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:13.580
If you own a sweets shop, I wonder if you get to eat

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:13.580
expired candy all the time.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:16.660
Didn't he give these to us

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:16.660
because he was tired of eating them himself?

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:17.790
Oh!

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:21.370
Then maybe someday I'll own a sweets shop

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:21.370
on shopping street!

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:23.000
When you do, give me sweets.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.910
Don't worry, I will!

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:28.790
Hello, I am Tin-Coin Sat-chan.

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:30.790
Where does the coin part come from?

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:33.160
What should we use that tin-tin for?

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:38.000
I know! We'll make a time capsule!

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:41.870
Oh, good idea! I definitely like the time capsule idea!

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:42.870
Nice thinking.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:45.370
How many years should we wait to open it?

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:47.750
Let's open it when we're grownups!

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:49.160
Like after ten years?

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:51.000
Ten years...

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.910
Okay, how many things should we put in?

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:55.040
Let's do number two!

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:56.790
Let's each put in three things.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:59.660
Got it! Three things!

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:09.080
To me in 10 years

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:09.080
Yui has her twinkler, one of Colonel Monochrome's

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:09.080
whiskers, and a letter to herself.

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:14.250
You

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:14.250
Win

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:14.250
One

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:13.910
Sat-chan brought a winning popsicle stick,

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:13.910
orange seeds, and ten yen.

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:21.040
And Koto-chan brought a game,

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:21.040
a flier from the supermarket, and a picture of us!

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.750
Okay, I'm putting them in!

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.160
Let me read your letter, Yui! Come on!

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:28.290
No! It's a secret until ten years from now.

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:29.950
To me in 10 years

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.950
Are you sure you want

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.950
to put that game in there, Kotoha?

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.410
Yeah. This one's kind of hard.

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:37.870
I'm going to let future me beat it.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.580
But every game is hard for you, Kotoha.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:46.620
Okay, I'm closing the capsule!

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:47.790
Okay!

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.120
Now time has stopped.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:53.500
Alright, let's go bury it!

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:55.830
Yeah!

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.830
But where should we bury it?

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:11.040
It has to be someplace with an obvious landmark.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.950
Something really big, that we won't forget.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:17.330
A landmark, a landmark...

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:18.700
Oh! I know!

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:20.830
Zoo Front Police Box

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:26.540
If we bury it here, Saito can be our landmark!

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:28.290
He's pretty big!

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:32.410
But will Saito-san still be there in ten years?

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:34.450
I sure hope not.

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:36.910
He's looking this way!

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.870
He's after our time capsule!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.330
Does he want to steal the winning popsicle stick?

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:42.750
It's possible.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.500
He's a greedy man.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:48.330
Maybe we should go somewhere else.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.250
Good idea. This was a bad spot.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.040
I don't know what that was about,

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:56.700
but I get the feeling I just prevented

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:56.700
something stupid before it happened.

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:02.080
Aren't there any good spots?

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:05.500
With a big landmark that we won't forget.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:09.080
Landmark, landmark...

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:13.000
How about this tree?

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:21.450
It's big! Probably the biggest!

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:23.580
Let's bury it under this tree!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.500
We can't work with a "probably"!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:29.000
We don't even know if this tree

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:29.000
will still be here in ten years.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:30.580
That's true.

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:34.120
They're always doing construction in this park.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:35.830
It's Nono-chan!

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.160
Yoohoo! Whatcha doing?

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:41.450
Something about ten years from now? Sounds fun.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:43.830
We made a time capsule!

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.330
Cool!

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:47.750
We're going to dig it back up in ten years.

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:49.870
Wow, that sounds nice.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:54.750
Come to think of it,

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:54.750
I've never done anything like that.

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:57.120
Then do you want to

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:57.120
put something in it, too, Nono-chan?

00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:58.750
What? Can I?

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:00.700
You're our friend, Nonoka.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.450
We'll make an exception for you.

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:05.290
You make Nonoka very happy!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:10.370
Oh, so you have pictures and stuff.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.080
Then I'll do that, too.

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:17.830
Let's use this one.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:22.040
A picture of me when I was little.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:26.950
Wow, Nonoka, you carry around pictures

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:26.950
of yourself as a kid?

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:28.620
That's creepy.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:30.290
Why would you...?

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:31.870
Let's not be her friend anymore.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.540
Try to spare my feelings, why don't you?!

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:38.250
That's the oldest picture I have of me eating bread.

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.120
You sure like bread, Nono-chan.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:43.330
I do!

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:46.750
But back then, I didn't like it very much yet.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:51.160
Thinking about it, this was exactly ten years ago.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:53.200
Another ten years, huh?

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.500
I wonder what I'll be doing then.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:57.250
Okay! Time to bury it!

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:58.870
Hey, wait a minute!

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:02.120
You weren't going to bury this tin,

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:02.120
just like that, were you?

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:03.660
Huh? Why not?

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:05.410
The can will decompose.

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:07.750
Cans...

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:09.080
...can decompose?

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:13.500
So you're giving it to me to hold on to?

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:15.790
You'll be our landmark!

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:17.950
You're the biggest.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.910
And we'll never forget you!

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:22.370
Pretty please?

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:25.200
A time capsule, huh?

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:27.660
We'll come get it in ten years, okay?

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:28.580
Got it.

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:30.830
You better live a long life, Pops!

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:33.200
Long life, huh?

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.500
Yeah, I better.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:41.200
Ueno Okachimachi Chudo-dori

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.620
Wait, I'm not that old, you know!

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:44.160
But you are a Pops.

00:20:44.160 --> 00:20:45.330
You are.

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:46.830
You're a Pops!

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:49.750
See you later, Pops!

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:52.120
Take care of yourself for ten years!

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:57.410
Ten years, huh?

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.120
That'll be no time at all.

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.750
Oh, but in ten years, Pops might've shrunk!

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:06.290
People do shrink.

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:08.620
But I don't want Pops to be little!

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:10.330
Me, neither.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:24.540
Our sparkling signal is the first star

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.580
Oops, time to go home

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:27.620
Later, Colors!

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:28.700
Later, Colors!

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:31.790
The peace is kept another day

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:32.540
We did it!

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:35.790
Total victory for us!

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:38.950
A chu-chu-cabrilla out on a walk

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:40.910
Take that! Extra virgin oil!

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:44.750
We're really busy every day

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:47.080
Cases from level one to how high?

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.080
We'll solve any mystery!

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:50.200
I've beat this game!

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:51.120
There it is!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.080
Call us again when you're in a pinch!

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:56.290
For the peace of this town!

00:21:56.450 --> 00:22:00.950
Saying, "Ready, go!" with the orange sky

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:04.870
Let's go home together

00:22:04.870 --> 00:22:09.080
Tomorrow we can probably have even more excitement

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:11.910
We all dash to meet at the hideout

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:17.160
Goodbye, sun. Goodnight, town

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:21.250
I can't wait for tomorrow

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:25.290
My heart won't stop skipping in excitement

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:29.620
Another day and all's well!

00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:32.200
See you tomorrow!

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:33.750
One more time!

00:22:33.750 --> 00:22:38.120
See you tomorrow!

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:45.410
Hewwo. I ahn Wa-Hoy Ui.

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:50.200
Weff har hoo-ay Hu-hurs Ee-wa-oo-

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:52.830
What's wrong, Leader?

00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:55.080
You dropped your coin already?

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:57.910
You have a long way to go

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:57.910
before you can be Colors Robot Mark 2.

00:22:57.910 --> 00:23:00.330
Well, it's actually really hard.

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:02.200
You try it, Kotoha.

00:23:02.200 --> 00:23:03.700
If you insist.

00:23:04.160 --> 00:23:06.790
Hewwo. I ahn Wa-Hoy-

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:10.580
That was worse than Leader!

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:12.830
You didn't even get as far as "one-coin"!

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:14.700
I don't need to do it.

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:16.950
I'm the one giving the orders to the Colors Robot.

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:20.000
What? I want to be the one giving orders, too.

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:22.120
Okay, Yui. You can give the first order.

00:23:22.120 --> 00:23:24.040
What? Um...

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:28.040
Okay, One-Coin Sat-chan!

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:28.040
Do the Colors Evaluation Meeting!

00:23:28.040 --> 00:23:29.290
You got it!

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:33.410
Hum hoo ho-ho! Hiss is heh hee-hoo

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:33.410
ho hee heff heh-heh-ho.

00:23:33.410 --> 00:23:37.330
Heh hwee, oo halla hway ah, ho-ho hwee ha hee.

00:23:37.330 --> 00:23:40.950
Hi hey oh hoo ha hey, hoo-ee ah ha!
